  {
    "id": "render-docker-dockerfile",
    "source_url": "https://render.com/docs/docker",
    "heading": "Building from a Dockerfile",
    "parent_context": "render / web-services / render-docker",
    "text": "Select Docker as the Render service language for a Dockerfile build, including Python applications. Configure Dockerfile Path when the file is outside the repository root. Docker Command can override the image CMD. Docker gives the application owner control over the base operating system and installed packages. Render builds from the repository Dockerfile. Cached mutable base-image tags may reuse an older image; the chosen image and dependencies must be reviewed when rebuilding.",
    "content_hash": "c360ce21535d58b3fb161f3d14f80643be3bc9b07cc31c53dd1b8051c9803cd9",
    "provider": "render",
