  {
    "id": "neon-restore-lifecycle",
    "source_url": "https://neon.com/docs/postgres/backup-restore/history-window",
    "heading": "History limits and recovery",
    "parent_context": "neon / postgresql / lifecycle",
    "text": "Neon documents a Free history window of six hours capped at 1 GB of history. Launch defaults to one day and supports up to seven days; Scale supports up to thirty days. Actual project settings determine recovery reach. A zero window disables instant restore and Time Travel. Paid history storage is separate from database storage and remains unmodeled here.",
